# libFuzzer dictionary for the `.docx` targets (`docx_reader`,
# `docx_roundtrip`) — issue #358. Passed as `-dict=dictionaries/docx.dict`
# by `.github/workflows/fuzz-nightly.yml`. Entries stay <= 64 bytes
# (libFuzzer skips longer words); `engine_fuzz::tests::
# docx_dictionary_is_well_formed` checks the syntax on stable.
#
# Names and values are WordprocessingML / DrawingML / Markup Compatibility
# vocabulary from ECMA-376 (Part 1 §17, §20; Part 3) — no foreign XML.
# They reach `word/document.xml` two ways: inside a raw ZIP input stored
# uncompressed (the `PK\x03\x04` path), and through `docx_gen`'s splice
# mode, whose raw-input splice copies a short slice of the fuzz input
# verbatim into the generated document at a tag boundary.

# Package / XML scaffolding
"PK\x03\x04"
"word/document.xml"
"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\" standalone=\"yes\"?>"
"xmlns:w=\""
"xmlns:r=\""
"xmlns:mc=\""
"xmlns:wp=\""
"xmlns:a=\""
"http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main"
"officeDocument/2006/relationships"
"http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
"drawingml/2006/wordprocessingDrawing"
"drawingml/2006/main"
"xml:space=\"preserve\""
"<![CDATA["
"]]>"
"<!--"
"-->"
"<?"
"?>"

